WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
Since 1988, Brazil's
space institute, INPE,

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.430
has measured forest clearing
in the Amazon every year.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.350
Amazonia holds roughly
16,000 tree species.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.370
At the forest edge, trees give
way to pasture for cattle.

5
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:22.300
In October 2023, the river at Manaus
fell to its lowest level since 1902.

6
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.150
Ranchers, miners and river
families all share this forest.

7
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.470
So why does change hit
each so differently?

8
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.610
In this mission, you'll
trace four kinds of change,

9
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.790
from clearing to drought,
and what drives them.

10
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.350
Then you'll judge how well
the responses are working,

11
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.570
for each group in turn.

12
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.410
Your mission: explain why
forest change hits ranchers,

13
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.120
miners and river families so differently.
